Article 63 Where an enterprise, public institution, or other producer or business operator commits any of the following acts, which does not yet constitute a crime, in addition to being penalized in accordance with the provisions of relevant laws and regulations, the environmental protection department of the people's government at or above the county level or another relevant department shall transfer the case to the public security organ, and shall impose on the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible persons a detention of not less than ten days but not more than fifteen days; where the circumstances are relatively minor, a detention of not less than five days but not more than ten days shall be imposed:
(1) failing to conduct environmental impact assessment for a construction project according to law, being ordered to stop construction but refusing to comply;
(2) failing to obtain a pollutant discharge permit to discharge pollutants in violation of the law, being ordered to stop discharging but refusing to comply;
(3) illegally discharging pollutants by evading supervision through means such as concealed pipes, seepage wells, seepage pits, perfusion, or tampering with or forging monitoring data, or operating pollution prevention facilities abnormally;
(4) producing or using pesticides that are explicitly prohibited from production or use by the State, being ordered to rectify but refusing to do so.

Article 68 Where a local people's government at any level, the environmental protection department of a people's government at or above the county level, or any other department vested with the function of environmental protection supervision and administration commits any of the following acts, the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible persons shall be given a disciplinary warning, a major demerit, or a demotion; if serious consequences are caused, they shall be removed from office or dismissed, and the principal responsible person shall resign to assume responsibility:
(1) granting an administrative license to a person who does not meet the conditions for such license;
(2) covering up an illegal environmental act;
(3) failing to make a decision on ordering suspension of business or closure as required by law;
(4) failing to timely investigate and deal with acts such as discharging pollutants exceeding the standards, discharging pollutants by evading supervision, causing environmental accidents, or failing to implement ecological protection measures causing ecological destruction, upon discovery or receipt of a report;
(5) sealing up or seizing the facilities or equipment of an enterprise, public institution, or other producer or business operator in violation of this Law;
(6) tampering with, forging, or directing others to tamper with or forge monitoring data;
(7) failing to publicly disclose environmental information as required by law;
(8) retaining, misappropriating, or diverting the collected pollutant discharge fees for other purposes;
(9) other illegal acts as provided for by laws and regulations.
